<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin heads for Paris to sign NATO accord.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin heads for Paris to sign NATO accord.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Boris Yeltsin left Moscow on Monday for Paris, where he is due to sign a pact with NATO setting out a new relationship with the western defence alliance, Russian news agencies said.</p>
<p>Yeltsin, who will sign a Founding Act with NATO leaders on Tuesday, said earlier that the accord stopped a slide towards confrontation sparked by NATO's plans to expand eastwards but could fall apart if NATO allowed in any former Soviet republics.</p>
</text>
